{"availability":"available","full":"amaranth-unm/campus-history","name":"campus-history","description":"Hosts a series of essays on the history of the UNM campus","category":"Other","language":"CSS","stars":0,"forks":15,"created":"2019-06-21T21:38:03Z","updated":"2026-10-08T17:07:33Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://amaranth-unm.github.io/campus-history/","topics":[],"demo":"https://amaranth.unm.edu/campus-history/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:12.097Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:12.097Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:18:12.097Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T05:49:02.703Z","stars":0,"forks":15},{"at":"2026-10-05T05:50:14.282Z","stars":0,"forks":15},{"at":"2026-10-07T11:14:24.643Z","stars":0,"forks":15},{"at":"2026-10-09T13:18:12.097Z","stars":0,"forks":15}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A student-driven digital history collaboration. UNM Campus Histories collects student-built essays about the buildings, landscapes, public art, and everyday places that shape university life at the University of New Mexico, turning explorations of UNM's official archive into a shared public record.","The project treats coursework as something that can outlast the semester. Instead of Word documents discarded when the course ends, students publish research that keeps circulating — and in the process learn version control, collaborative editing, and scholarly publishing on open-source tools. The site doubles as a model for how digital humanities projects can be public, collaborative, and sustainable without servers, licences, or hosting costs."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amaranth-unm/campus-history/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"1c79465dcc0d49eaf25a78fbf520314e7143d3ef3610f04157cfedf977c2f68f","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T05:06:09.213Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T11:16:14.765Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A student-driven digital histo